    "readme_description": "Given an integer array `nums`, return *the number of **AND triples***.\n\nAn **AND triple** is a triple of indices `(i, j, k)` such that:\n\n- `0 <= i < nums.length`\n- `0 <= j < nums.length`\n- `0 <= k < nums.length`\n- `nums[i] & nums[j] & nums[k] == 0`, where `&` represents the bitwise-AND operator.",
